    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d137">

                <pb facs="0359" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg101"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.0151/42</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 12, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.25 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1631. Your telegram 1106 [1105], February 10, taken up with Sir Edward Grey and a memorandum embodying its
                    request left with <pb facs="0360" n="102" xml:id="pg102"/> him. He said that the
                    Admiralty had already received instructions which he thought practically
                    complied with our request but that he would answer more specifically as soon as
                    he could confer with the Cabinet and the Admiralty.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
